        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seekonk%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was incorporated in 1812, carved out of the western half of Rehoboth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seekonk%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before settlers arrived, the Wampanoag people called the area Seekonk, meaning “People of the Morning Light.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seekonk%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Seekonk’s public library, located near Route 152, has been a community hub for generations.",
